onzales's April resignation, and Republicans enter the general with the advantage. Brandon Herrera, a firearms-content creator who battled Gonzales in the GOP primary, has raised nearly $2 million and holds a clear financial edge over Democrat Katy Padilla Stout, though outside groups have spent heavily against him.\n\nThe race is closer than the district's lean suggests. A Democratic-friendly midterm environment, Herrera's widely covered crude and extremist remarks, and Democratic targeting of the San Antonio and border-area seat have kept it competitive; prediction markets put Democratic win odds near 40%. Most expert raters still call the district Likely or Lean Republican, and the only available polls are months-old partisan surveys showing a narrow Republican lead. The expectation is a Republican hold by a modest margin, with real upside for Democrats if the national environment strengthens.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}]}